{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"endDynamics"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNonNegativeDecimal","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL21MXLNonNegativeDecimala","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNonNegativeDecimal"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"end-dynamics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/endDynamics"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Note Off velocity, corresponding to MIDI 1.0’s Note Off velocity, expressed as a percentage of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default forte value (90 for MIDI 1.0)."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/enddynamics"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV11endDynamicsSdSgvp","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"endDynamics"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNonNegativeDecimal","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL21MXLNonNegativeDecimala"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","title":"endDynamics"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/endDynamics":{"title":"endDynamics","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"endDynamics","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNonNegativeDecimal","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL21MXLNonNegativeDecimala"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/endDynamics","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/enddynamics","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Note Off velocity, corresponding to MIDI 1.0’s Note Off velocity, expressed as a percentage of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default forte value (90 for MIDI 1.0)."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"title":"MXLNote","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNonNegativeDecimal":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNonNegativeDecimal"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNonNegativeDecimal","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLNonNegativeDecimal","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNonNegativeDecimal","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnonnegativedecimal","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The non-negative-decimal type specifies a non-negative decimal value."}]}}}